"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D158 makes each attempt to explain the strange situation become a prompt for the next practical task.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"D156 seeks surrender of an ordinary explanation; D158 can leave beliefs unresolved while redirecting the conversation into action.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Original A3 and A5 turn metaphysical objections into feeding decisions; revised A3 and A5 also use B's lateness and car departure.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a commandeers a housemate's commute for hospitality; alternative b bargains with a colleague who wants to protect a gallery floor.\",\n      \"reason\": \"The original narrowly missed acceptance because B only supplied disbelief. Added a shared lateness problem and commute. Internal reread: fidelity 5 (A3 and A5 redirect why questions), logic 5 (A3 uses B2's lateness; A5 uses B4's car), relationship 4 (B wants to leave), heightening 4 (A5 adds transport), specificity 4 (A1 gives breakfast), brevityWit 4 (A5 makes the cemetery a practical stop): 90.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The cemetery destination is newly supplied by A5; its connection to the ghost is clear but remains an assumption rather than an established preference.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D158-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"824d380bfbc674a82f9f816f4a3a9b7aacd1d7aa31b7cd6578f516484d994cc2\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 redirects B2's question to the carpet, but A5 delivers a maxim rather than specifying what must happen next.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 uses B2's painting, while A5 answers B4's generic impossibility without receiving new practical pressure.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 only express astonishment; neither establishes why B resists holding the bucket.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5 returns to the same bucket requested in A1 rather than developing containment.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 supplies a leak and bucket, and B2 identifies the painting as the source.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 is compact but aphoristic, with little new practical action.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 62\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Hold this bucket under the seascape. I'll get towels before the gallery floor floods.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Why is a painting leaking? I said we should buy a print.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You can choose the replacement. Tilt the bucket toward the waves.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Why are there fish? This bucket's nearly full.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Fetch the aquarium from reception. I'll hold this one until you're back.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D158 redirects inquiries about the impossible situation's existence into immediate practical responses.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"A merely unflappable character may ignore the weirdness; D158 actively converts B's questions into tasks.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Revised A3 answers B2's purchase grievance with replacement authority and containment; A5 converts B4's fish question into an aquarium request.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"The ghost alternative uses an imminent departure to recruit transport; this version bargains over replacement art and shares the containment work.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Specified a new gallery setting and gave B purchasing history and a filling bucket. Internal reread: fidelity 5 (A3 and A5 redirect both why questions), logic 5 (A3 uses the print grievance; A5 uses B4's fish and capacity), relationship 4 (B gains replacement choice), heightening 4 (A5 adds live-animal containment), specificity 4 (A1 establishes floor protection), brevityWit 4 (A5's aquarium follows the fish): 90.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The reception aquarium is convenient new equipment; the scene would be slightly stronger in performance if that resource felt familiar to both colleagues.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D159-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"46273fb84a085f7bf14fafc4ed663aee8ef4215c0f9dc9eb67790ecf04e34beb\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A1 offers preparation and B4 exposes concealment, but B's hope and practical supporting evidence are absent.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 responds to B2's calculation; A5 answers B4's covered number by naming no actual next task.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"B2 appears to reject arrival, so A's supposed protection of B's hope lacks a personal basis.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A5 vaguely redirects attention instead of increasing useful preparation or protective concealment.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 identifies a future visitor and chair, but the visitor's importance to B is unspecified.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3's pessimistic calculation is concise personification; A5's 'next useful task' is editorial abstraction.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 48\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Your daughter's voice came through from tomorrow. Bring her chair beside the machine.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Do you think she can come through too?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Her voice crossed. Bring the cushion she likes.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Why's her photo covering 'arrival: zero percent'?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I'd rather see her face. Hold the photo while I clear her landing space; she'll want to recognize this room.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D159 makes A protect B's hope through partial evidence and practical preparation while quietly obscuring a concrete reason for pessimism.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"D158 redirects questions into tasks without needing protective intent or adverse knowledge; D159's redirection preserves B's personally invested hope while concealing bad evidence.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"B2 hopes for a daughter's arrival, A3 cites the voice as partial evidence, and B4 identifies an explicitly discouraging estimate hidden under her photo before A5 redirects into preparation.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This alternative protects an intimate reunion hope through familiar belongings and arrival preparations; alternative b protects an inventor's demonstration by redirecting attention from a stated capacity limit to a small visible success.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Kept the temporal reunion and made the covered estimate's content explicit, repairing the rejected candidate's ambiguous adverse information. Original firstPass remains unchanged. Separate internal reread: fidelity 4 (A3 supplies partial evidence and B4 exposes A's concealment), logic 5 (A3 answers B2's hope; A5 repurposes the photo B4 questions while continuing arrival preparations), relationship 4 (B2 wants reunion and B4 challenges reassurance), heightening 4 (A5 commits to a landing space despite the exposed estimate), specificity 5 (A1 supplies the machine and A3 a familiar cushion), brevityWit 4 (A5's preference for her face is a concise protective evasion): 87. Five spoken ABABA turns; arrival and B's acceptance remain unresolved.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"B4 discovers the discouraging fact, so the withholding is an exposed attempt rather than successful concealment. A3's voice evidence